## What this predicate means

**A `specializes` B** — A is a sub-property of B; A is a NARROWER version of the relation B expresses.  Property-level analog of `extends` (which is class-level).

Per RDFS rule rdfs7, declaring `A specializes B` entails: for every fact `x A y`, the fact `x B y` also holds.  Entailment propagates upward in the property hierarchy.

Examples:
- `:mm.memory/evidences specializes :mm.memory/cites` (evidence is a stronger form of citation)
- `:mm.memory/triggered-by specializes :mm.memory/motivated-by` (direct trigger is a stronger form of motivation)
- `:mm.memory/motivated-by specializes :mm.memory/informed-by`

